variables ...) and sends back what it finds once. Explain in comments inside the code, briefly; never think
aloud in comments. Ladder is rung text, one rung per line ending with ; and [A ,B ] is a branch (OR):
    [XIC(Start) ,XIC(Motor) ]XIC(Stop)OTE(Motor);
XIC is true while the input is on, XIO while it is off. A normally closed Stop button (or overload contact) keeps
its input on until it is pressed (or trips), so it is examined with XIC; XIO there would never let the motor run.
